[W4b WHY THE WIDTH STOPS WHERE IT DOES — a theorem of the committed layer, stated and then verified on every record built here]
  THEOREM (the branching bound).  Let a record's events carry at
  most B registers each (`regs_of`).  Then for every event e and
  every depth d >= 1, the SKY-B chart satisfies |D_e(d)| <= B^d.
  Proof.  Write R_e(k) = {f : e <= f, h[f] = h[e] + k} for the
  REFLEXIVE k-layer (so R_e(0) = {e}, R_e(k) = D_e(k) for k >= 1,
  and R_e(k) = {} for k < 0).  `event_poset` sets pred[j] =
  U_{r in regs(j)} (pred[last[r]] u {last[r]}), so the order is
  the transitive closure of the relation P: x P y iff x is the
  immediately preceding event on some register of y.  Each P-step
  raises height by at least 1, and each x has at most
  |regs(x)| <= B P-successors (one per register, the next event
  on that wire).  Hence for k >= 1, R_e(k) = U_{y : e P y}
  R_y(k - (h[y] - h[e])): every f > e is reached from e by a
  P-path, whose first step is some such y.  Induct on k: the
  union has at most B terms, each of size at most B^{k-1}
  because h[y] - h[e] >= 1.  So |R_e(k)| <= B^k, and D_e(d) =
  R_e(d).  []
  CONSEQUENCE, and it is the wall: a record made of DELIVERIES
  has B = 2 (carriers {s, r}), so max |D| <= 4 at d = 2 and <= 8
  at d = 3 — NO delivery circuit whatever can reach the
  sprinklings' max |D| 10-17.  Width beyond 4 at
  d = 2 needs events with 3+ registers, and the layer has exactly
  one such species: an ARBITRATION over a component with 2+
  distinct proposers (regs = proposers u {new version}).  So at
  grammar layer chart width past 4 is bought with CONFLICT, not
  with transport.
  registers per event species (committed `regs_of`): proposal 1, idle 1, delivery 2, merge 2, arbitration = #proposers + 1 — the exhibited two-proposer arb is admissible (q = 1/8) and carries 3 registers
  [PASS] W4b THE WIDTH WALL IS STRUCTURAL AND THE DOUBLE RING SATURATES IT.  Every record built in this unit obeys |D| <= B^d with B the record's own maximum register count, and B = 2 IS NOW GATED, not asserted (round-1 MINOR 6: max |regs_of(e)| measured on every event of every record, mint prefix included) — and the bound is TIGHT: the coupled rings hit max |D| = 4 = 2^2 at d = 2 exactly, which is why D60's 3 was beatable and why nothing here reaches the sprinklings' 10-17 at d = 2.  What W4b licenses is a NECESSITY: |D| >= 5 at d = 2 REQUIRES a 3+-register event, i.e. an arbitration over 2+ distinct proposers (round-1 MINOR 3 — whether a record CARRYING such width exists is open, residue 1); the exhibited admissible 3-register arbitration shows only that the wall is a fact about DELIVERY CIRCUITS, not about the grammar  (records checked = 38, bound violations = 0, B values measured = [2], saturating configurations = 26 (e.g. ('DR', 4, 10, 4, 1)); brick max|D| = 3, winner max|D| = 4, bound 2^2 = 4, sprinklings 10-17)

